   {
    "title": "The Wise Vote",
    "description": "The website pulls data from various APIs that yields a site robust with data and information for various members of congress and current issues. Many of the design choices revolve around assignment specifications and will most likely change once class has ended to better fit our individual vision - designs that disregard grade deductions\n\nI work on the Front-end of the site - dealing with React components and CSS to also create a mobile-friendly experience.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Feb 2019 - Present"
   },
   {
    "title": "Pintos",
    "description": "Project is stored in a private repo in GitHub for academic purposes. The project included:\n- add thread prioritization and changed the toy OS from single-threaded to multi-threaded\n- had user programs add onto the stack and gave them the ability to make use of system calls\n- added virtual memory functionality to allow multiple user programs to run. This included the use of on-demand paging (instead of pre-paging) and a swap partition\n- implemented a multi-level index file system to support small and very large files",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Sep 2018 - Dec 2018"
